-- title:
--   Independence of the local Hecke algebra of the avoided primes
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, complete for the $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$-adic topology, let $p$ be a prime with $p \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}(\mathcal{O})$, i.e. a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\sigma \mapsto \bar\rho(\sigma)$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field; assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, meaning that its base change to $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,k$ has no invariant submodules besides $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S_1 \subseteq S$ be finite sets of naturals with $p \in S_1$, and let $N \neq 0$ be such that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S_1$, with the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ spanned over $\mathbb{C}$ by forms with integral $q$-coefficients (the `Fact` that [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6) holds). Here [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ (so for $S_1$, and hence for $S$, no $U$-operators occur). Let $\theta_1 : \mathbb{T}^{S_1} \to k$ be a ring homomorphism such that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S_1$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x \mapsto x^\ell$, one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \theta_1(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $\theta : \mathbb{T}^{S} \to k$ be the composite of $\theta_1$ with the inclusion $\mathbb{T}^{S} \subseteq \mathbb{T}^{S_1}$ arising from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_mono`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L45) and $S_1 \subseteq S$. Finally let $\Psi$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₁ 𝒪 θ₁`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) — localisations of the algebras `heckeBaseAlgebra N S 𝒪`, respectively for $S$ and $S_1$, at the images under `latticeBaseChange` of the complements of the primes `heckeCharKernel N S 𝒪 θ` and `heckeCharKernel N S₁ 𝒪 θ₁` — such that $\Psi$ carries $\pi(t)$ to $\pi_1$ of the image of $t$ under that inclusion, for every $t \in \mathbb{T}^{S}$. Then $\Psi$ is bijective.
--
--   This is the independence of the localised weight-two Hecke algebra at a non-Eisenstein character from the auxiliary finite set of primes excluded from the Hecke algebra: enlarging the excluded set from $S_1$ to $S$ does not change the localisation. It is used whenever auxiliary primes are adjoined to the excluded set in the Taylor–Wiles argument, and is cited in the construction of algebra homomorphisms out of corner rings and in the level-lowering and degeneracy-map comparisons.
